r write or mid-save crash cannot durably lose the rotation max now that the inline floor is removed.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["binding_store.py:301-321 — save() does os.replace(bindings.json) at line 313 then get_rotation.save() at line 321","get_rotation.py:82-112 — save() is fail-open: returns False on OSError, never raises (confirmed by test_sidecar_tempfile_failure_does_not_abort_legacy_save)","merge_legacy (get_rotation.py:44-52) is the only recovery path for a lost sidecar advance, and it depends on the inline stamp still being present on disk — which A2-2 removes","Today the inline floor makes this window harmless; A2-2 removes the floor while sidecar persistence stays best-effort, opening a lose-progress window the plan claims cannot occur"],"finding":"The plan's 'persist the maximum to get_rotation.json before removing the inline field' is contradicted by the existing save ordering: BindingStore.save() commits bindings.json (with the inline field scrubbed) BEFORE the fail-open get_rotation.save(), so a fail-open sidecar write (or a crash between the two os.replace calls) durably loses the rotation max instead of self-healing.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4bf38b40f3766a0f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section ('persist that maximum to get_rotation.json before removing the inline field') and Compatibility gate ('self-heals instead of losing rotation progress')","norm_id":"nd76374fdb8208cae","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["Sidecar tempfile/os.replace fails open on the same save that scrubs the inline field","Process is killed (GHA runner eviction) between the bindings.json os.replace and the get_rotation.json os.replace"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Reorder BindingStore.save() so the sidecar is committed first and the inline field is only stripped from the in-memory bindings after get_rotation.save() returns True; if the sidecar persist fails open, retain the inline stamp for that key this pass. Add an integration test that fails the sidecar write during the scrub pass and asserts rotation order is preserved on reload.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the post-rollback behavior for a downgrade below the A2-1 sidecar floor: assert that a pre-sidecar binary observing scrubbed inline stamps only forfeits bounded rotation optimization (self-heals within ceil(N/K), no correctness loss), and scope the 'downgrade recovery' claim to sidecar-aware binaries.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'This is the irreversible half of A2.'","Plan: 'The read-only fallback ... preserves downgrade/mixed-writer recovery' — but the recovery seam (get_rotation.latest = max(sidecar, legacy)) is only exercised by sidecar-aware binaries; a pre-A2-1 binary reads only entry['last_get_pass'].","ABSENCE: no acceptance criterion or gate line states what rotation state a pre-sidecar binary observes after inline is scrubbed, nor bounds the resulting loss.","Impact is bounded: rotation is fail-open (get_rotation.load treats absent/malformed state as empty; loss costs a bounded extra GET) and anti-starvation still holds per AC line 2, so this is churn/optimization loss, not correctness data loss."],"finding":"The plan labels A2-2 'the irreversible half' and performs a one-way inline-field scrub, but does not explicitly assert the post-rollback state for a downgrade to a PRE-A2-1 (pre-sidecar) binary — one that reads only inline last_get_pass and knows nothing of get_rotation.json. After A2-2 scrubs inline stamps, that older binary would observe empty rotation state. The retained max(sidecar, legacy) recovery seam only aids binaries aware of the sidecar, so the plan's 'preserves downgrade/mixed-writer recovery' claim does not cover a downgrade below the sidecar-capable floor.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f38b121dca02ae5e0","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Compatibility and evidence gate' and 'Approach' sections; AC line 4 (operator-attested gate)","norm_id":"n91c9abe2ae10226c","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Operators roll the reconciler/probe deployment back to a build older than the A2-1 merge after A2-2 has scrubbed inline stamps from bindings.json.","An overlooked pre-A2-1 process (not merely a mixed old/new sidecar-aware writer) resumes and sees empty rotation history."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In the Compatibility gate, add: the writer-upgrade gate defines the rollback floor as any build >= the A2-1 merge; add an acceptance/operator note that downgrading below that floor forfeits only bounded rotation-optimization state (fail-open, self-healing within ceil(N/K)) and never binding correctness, and that no writer below the A2-1 floor may be deployed after A2-2.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_acc